# Line endings.
#
# Git for Windows defaults to core.autocrlf=true, which rewrites LF to
# CRLF on checkout. Every file here is consumed inside a Linux
# container, and several break on CRLF:
#
#   *.sh          a shebang of "#!/bin/sh\r" names an interpreter that
#                 does not exist, so the container exits 127
#   *.cbl, *.cpy  fixed-format COBOL is column-sensitive
#   iris.script   fed to `iris session` on stdin at build time
#   *.edi         partner messages are hashed for non-repudiation
#
# Normalising to LF in the working tree removes the whole class of
# problem regardless of how any attendee has configured Git.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Windows-only helpers would go here as eol=crlf. There are none today.
